# ROS2 Zenoh Project Rules

**Purpose:** Ensure consistent documentation, code quality, and AI governance across the project.

---

## Quick Reference

**Validation Commands:**
```bash
just validate   # All validations (lint, typecheck, frontmatter, specs, docs)
just fmt        # Format Python with Ruff
just test       # Run Python tests
just test-docs  # Test documentation code examples
just ci         # Full CI pipeline

# TypeScript documentation tools (primary validation)
cd typescript/ros2-zenoh-tools && npm run validate
```

**Create New Documents:**
```bash
just new-spec ComponentName       # Create new specification
just new-pattern PatternName      # Create new pattern
```

**Key Files:**
- `ruff.toml` - Python linting/formatting config (Ruff)
- `.markdownlint.yaml` - Markdown style rules
- `.yamllint.yaml` - YAML frontmatter rules
- `pyproject.toml` - Python workspace config
- `typescript/ros2-zenoh-tools/` - TypeScript documentation tools (primary validation)
- `tools/validate_*.py` - Legacy Python validation scripts

---

## Documentation Standards

### Universal Frontmatter Fields (All Markdown Files)

Every markdown file in `docs/` uses **structured frontmatter** (no explicit `id` field - IDs are derived):

```yaml
---
# Core Identity (ID is derived from type + name/number)
type: spec | adr | pattern | convention | tutorial | howto | concept
name: component-name                     # For specs, patterns, conventions (matches filename!)
number: "NNN"                            # For ADRs only (e.g., "002")
title: Human Readable Title              # 3-100 chars

# Classification & Governance
classification: public | internal | confidential | restricted
llm_processing: allowed | cloud-ok | on-prem-only | no-llm | review-required
schema_version: "1.0"

# Authorship
author: Name or Team                     # Optional, defaults to "Development Team"
maintainer: Name or Team                 # Optional, who maintains this
reviewed_by: Name                        # Optional, last reviewer

# Discoverability
summary: One-sentence summary            # Max 120 chars, for search/preview
tags: [tag1, tag2, tag3]                # Searchable keywords
---
```

**Field Definitions:**

**classification:**
- `public` - Can be shared externally, published online
- `internal` - Internal use only, not for external sharing
- `confidential` - Sensitive, restricted access, watermarked
- `restricted` - Highly sensitive, legal/compliance restrictions

**llm_processing:**
- `cloud-ok` - Can be sent to cloud LLMs (Claude, GPT-4, etc.)
- `on-prem-only` - Must use local/on-premises LLMs only
- `no-llm` - Do not process with LLMs (manual review only)
- `review-required` - LLM output must be human-reviewed before use

**Default if not specified:**
- classification: `internal`
- llm_processing: `allowed`
- schema_version: `"1.0"`

---

### ⚠️ CRITICAL: Wikilinks and Cross-References

**FOR LLMs**: Three separate systems - understand the difference!

#### 1. Wikilinks in Markdown Content
**Always use FILENAMES** (lowercase, without .md):
```markdown
✅ CORRECT:
See [[clock]] for core behavior.
See [[clock-python]] for Python API  
.
Follows [[002-three-time-modes]].

❌ WRONG - Don't use these:
[[spec:clock]]           # Not derived IDs!
[[Clock]]                # Not title case!
[[spec-clock]]           # Not with namespace prefix!
```

#### 2. Cross-References in Frontmatter
**Use just names/numbers** (no namespace prefix):
```yaml
✅ CORRECT:
related_specs: [clock, rate]           # Just names
related_adrs: [002, 005]               # Just numbers
related_patterns: [fixed-rate-loop]    # Just names

❌ WRONG:
related_specs: ["spec:clock"]    # Don't include namespace!
related_specs: [[clock]]         # Not wikilinks in YAML!
```

#### 3. Derived IDs (For Tools Only)
Tools derive IDs automatically - **you never write them**:
- `type: spec, name: clock` → `spec:clock`
- `type: adr, number: "002"` → `adr:002`
- `type: pattern, name: fixed-rate-loop` → `pattern:fixed-rate-loop`

#### 4. Filename MUST Match Name Field
```yaml
# ✅ File: clock.md
name: clock                 # Matches!

# ✅ File: clock-python.md
name: clock-python          # Matches!

# ✅ File: 002-three-time-modes.md
type: adr
number: "002"              # ADRs use number, not name

# ❌ File: my-clock.md
name: clock                # Doesn't match - ERROR!
```

