### Specification Frontmatter (docs/06-Specs/*.md)

Component specifications include additional fields:

```yaml
---
# Core (from universal)
id: spec:<component-name>
title: Component Name Specification
type: reference
updated: YYYY-MM-DD

# Classification (from universal)
classification: public | internal | confidential | restricted
llm_processing: cloud-ok | on-prem-only | no-llm | review-required
license: MIT

# Spec-Specific
category: spec
domain: <domain>.<subdomain>             # e.g., "testing.mocks", "safety.collision"
pattern: pattern:<pattern-name>          # Which pattern this follows
version: "X.Y"                           # Semantic version
status: draft | review | approved | implemented | deprecated
generate: true | false                   # Is this generatable?
derived_from: <source-path-or-empty>    # What this was extracted from

# Safety & Compliance
safety_critical: true | false            # Safety-critical component?
security_sensitive: true | false         # Handles sensitive data?
compliance: []                           # e.g., [MISRA, ISO26262, GDPR]
hazard_level: none | low | medium | high | critical

# Lifecycle
deprecated_by: spec:<replacement>        # If deprecated, what replaces it?
deprecation_date: YYYY-MM-DD            # When was it deprecated?
eol_date: YYYY-MM-DD                    # When will it be removed?

# Relationships
depends_on: []                           # IDs of dependencies
related: []                              # IDs of related specs
supersedes: spec:<old-spec>             # If this replaces another

# Implementation Tracking
implementation:
  python: implemented | in-progress | planned | n/a
  rust: implemented | in-progress | planned | n/a
  c: implemented | in-progress | planned | n/a
  typescript: implemented | in-progress | planned | n/a

# External References
issue: "#123"                            # GitHub issue
pr: "#456"                               # GitHub PR
epic: "PROJ-789"                        # Jira epic (if applicable)
---
```

